# Dev logs

When the user reports a cast, browser, pairing, VPN, or workspace problem on Fire TV or Windows:

1. Run `.\tools\scripts\pull-dev-logs.ps1` (optional `-Serial host:5555`, `-ClearLogcat` after they reproduce).
2. Read `artifacts/logs/session-meta.txt`, then `firetv-latest.log`, then `windows-latest.log`.
3. Do not invent device behaviour that contradicts those logs.

Windows app writes continuously to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Flint\logs\windows-latest.log` via `DevFileLog`
(`FlintDiag` breadcrumbs: cast/trust/browser/workspace/VPN/session/UI). The file is size-capped
(trim oldest → keep newest). Avalonia binding TRACE is filtered. Fire TV uses `Log.*` tags
(`FlintReceiver`, `FlintBrowser`, `FlintWorkspace`, `FlintVpn*`, `BrowserTlsServer`); pull filters
those. Never log or paste secrets (VPN config, keys, cookies, passwords, PEMs, preview pixels,
page text).
